Third-party material in this repository, and what LICENSE does NOT cover
=======================================================================

LICENSE grants MIT over this project. This file names the material inside the
repository that is NOT this project's to grant, and withholds it from that
grant. It only ever takes away. Nothing here adds a permission.

WHY THIS IS A SEPARATE FILE AND NOT A PARAGRAPH IN LICENSE

Because appending it to LICENSE would silently revoke the whole grant. GitHub's
licence detector matches LICENSE against the canonical MIT text and returns
NOASSERTION when anything follows it — this repository has already been through
that exact failure and wrote the lesson down in LICENSE-HARDWARE: "Put the
clarification beside the licence, never inside it." It matters more here than
cosmetics, because this repo is the seed of the Wish It Better network and that
network's second criterion is "a LICENSE with a real SPDX identifier", read from
the licence API. A carve-out written in good faith in the wrong file would fail
the project against the rule it wrote.


